l.md","source":"https://github.com/sarja-technologies/yaob"},"install_md":"Yaob comes as its source code plus eight model files. A script downloads the files, checks every checksum and puts the core back together.\n\n1. Get the code. You need Python 3.12 or newer.\n\n   ```\n   git clone https://github.com/sarja-technologies/yaob\n   cd yaob\n   python3 -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate\n   pip install -e '.[model]'\n   ```\n\n2. Download and check the model files (9.3 GB):\n\n   ```\n   scripts/fetch_release.sh ~/yaob\n   ```\n\n3. Import the network and start Yaob. The [install guide](https://github.com/sarja-technologies/yaob/blob/main/docs/install.md) has the two commands, and how to ask questions from the command line or any OpenAI-compatible app.\n\n   On a 12 GB graphics card, run `mpn budget set context_tokens=4096`, so a long request is refused instead of running out of memory. With less than 32 GB of system memory, also run `mpn budget set reserve_gib=4`: by default Yaob keeps 16 GiB free for other programs and refuses requests that would cut into it.","files":[{"name":"yaob-n10k-0.1.0.tar.gz","url":"https://github.com/sarja-technologies/yaob/releases/download/v0.1.0/yaob-n10k-0.1.0.tar.gz","bytes":45621685,"sha256":"bc2f831f090e2c25c57860f54885600470ce1def99cbd105e2f79c7094bbdd5c","role":"file","platform":"Linux","arch":"x86-64, ARM64","format":"Knowledge network and router","optional":false,"mirrors":[]},{"name":"yaob-n10k-0.1.0-specialists-experimental.tar.gz","url":"https://github.com/sarja-technologies/yaob/releases/download/v0.1.0/yaob-n10k-0.1.0-specialists-experimental.tar.gz","bytes":1024441454,"sha256":"57b101cc5b376c93b388efb61cd105548c1c95589de1fcd2ceb607759de1f8ab","role":"file","platform":"Linux","arch":"x86-64, ARM64","format":"Network with 4 specialist adapters","optional":true,"mirrors":[]},{"name":"qwen3-4b-instruct-2507-cdbee75f.tar.part-aa","url":"https://github.com/sarja-technologies/yaob/releases/download/v0.1.0/qwen3-4b-instruct-